    "result_text": "Grades are now dated, and `bin/e2e` passes (1 test, 1 passed).\n\n**What changed**\n- **Stored data:** a new migration, `V19__person_grade.sql`, adds a `person_grade` table that keeps each person's grades with their from-dates. Existing grades are copied in with no from-date, so they apply from the beginning of time. The old `person.grade` column is dropped.\n- **Server:**\n  - A person's first grade always applies from the beginning of time, whatever date is given.\n  - A later save records the grade from the form's from-date, or the sheet's today if none is given. It replaces any grade already recorded for that same date and keeps the rest.\n  - An invalid from-date is refused with the form's existing error.\n  - Settling a claim and closing a period both use the grade in force on the claim's date.\n  - An import records each grade from the sheet's today.\n  - The people list returns the grade in force on the sheet's today, plus the full grade history.\n  - The `PERSON_EDITED` / `PERSON_ADDED` audit lines show the grade that save recorded, so the line format is unchanged.\n- **Front end:** the person form has a new date field (`person-form-grade-from`) that defaults to the sheet's today. A claim's due uses the person's grade on the claim's date.\n\n**Behaviour you might not expect**\n- **Due-total rule widened:** a person's due-total used to show \"n/a\" whenever their current grade had no rate, unless a settled claim kept a figure. The test needs 3.00 here, so claims dated under an earlier grade that had a rate now keep their figures too. For anyone whose grade never changed, the rule works exactly as before.\n- **Unchanged grades aren't re-recorded:** if the chosen grade is already in force on the from-date, nothing new is stored. This means editing only a name doesn't add a duplicate grade entry dated today.\n\nThe front-end build doesn't type-check, so my first attempt failed at runtime on a missing import. I added an `npx tsc --noEmit` check, which now passes.",
